Who is the most important person in the kingdom?
When the disciples came to Jesus, they asked him, saying, "Who is the greatest in the kingdom of the heavens?"
And Jesus called a small child, and he set him in their midst.
Jesus said, "What I tell you is the truth. You must change and become like little children. If you do not, you will never enter the kingdom of heaven."
When a child like this becomes humble, he is the greatest in the Kingdom of Heaven.
Whoever receives a child like him in my name receives me.
But if one of these little ones who believe in me is led astray, it would be better for him to have a great millstone fastened around his neck and to be drowned in the depths of the sea.
How intense is the temptation of the world because of things that cause people to enter into disobedience! And it is inevitable that such things will come. But woe to those because of whom they come!
If your hand or foot causes you to stumble, cut it off and throw it away. It is better for you to enter life maimed than to have two hands or two feet and be thrown into eternal fire, where 'their worm does not die, and the fire is not quenched' (Isaiah 66:24).
If your right eye causes you to stumble, tear it out and throw it away. It is better for you to enter the kingdom of God with only one eye than to have two eyes and be thrown into the fire of hell. The parable of the lost sheep.
Look, lest you should despise one of these little ones. For I tell you, that in heaven their angels always see the face of my Father which is in heaven.
