Jesus rules over the Pharisees and the scribes.
Jesus spoke to the crowds and his disciples.
He said, "The secretaries and Pharisees sit on the seat of Moses."
You must obey them. Do everything they command you to do. But do not do what they do. They do not apply what they say.
They tie heavy loads and place them on people's shoulders. And they themselves do not move a finger for a little bit of effort in moving them.
All they do is to be seen by others. On their foreheads and arms they put small boxes containing verses from the Bible. They make these boxes very broad. And they make the embroidery ribbons on their coats very long.
They love to sit in places of honor at banquets. And to be at the forefront in gatherings.
They like to be greeted with "Peace be upon you" in the markets of the country. They are pleased when someone calls them "my Lord".
But it should not be called usury by anyone among you, for you have one Father,
Do not call anyone on earth your father. For you have one Father, and He is in heaven.
You should not have been called teacher. You have one teacher, the Christ.
The most important person among you will be your servant.
He who exalts himself will be humbled, and he who is humbled will be exalted.
Woe to you, you scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! For you shut the kingdom of heaven in people's faces. You neither enter yourselves nor do you allow those who would enter to do so!
