How grievous your loss, you scribes and Pharisees, you hypocrites! For you traverse sea and land to make a single convert, and when he has become one, you make him twice as much a child of hell as yourselves.
How great is your error, you who blind others! For you say: If anyone swears by the Temple of God, it is nothing; but if anyone swears by the gold of the Temple, he is bound by his oath!
You are blind and foolish! What is more important? The gold or the temple which sanctifies the gold?
You also say: "If anyone swears by the altar, he is not bound to it. But if anyone swears by the offering placed on it, he is bound to it."
O ye blind! What is the more important thing? Is it the gift or the altar which sanctifies the gift?
Whoever swears by God, his oath is by God. And whoever swears by the covenant of God, his oath is by God and by what is adjacent to Him.
And everyone who swears by the name of the temple swears by the temple and by the God who dwells in it.
And whoever swears by the heavens has indeed sworn by the throne of Allah and whoever is upon it.
But woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you tithe mint and dill and cumin, and yet neglect the weightier matters of the law: justice and mercy and faithfulness. You should have done these, without neglecting the others.
O patients of the hearts! Those who pick out the hair from the food. And they swallow the camel in one gulp
Woe to you, teachers of the law and Pharisees, you hypocrites! You clean the outside of the cup and dish, but inside they are full of greed and self-indulgence. Blind guides! You strain out a gnat but swallow a camel. Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! You build tombs for the prophets and decorate the tombs of the righteous. You say, 'If we had lived in the days of our ancestors, we would not have participated in their bloodshed. We would have warned them to stop their murderous ways.' You testify against yourselves that you are the descendants of those who murdered the prophets. Fill up, then, the measure of the sins of your ancestors! "I am sending you Elijah the prophet before the great and dreadful day of the Lord comes. He will turn the hearts of the parents to their children, and the hearts of the children to their parents; or else I will come and strike the land with a curse."
Blind, oh you Pharisees! Clean first the outside of the cup and of the platter, that they may be clean also to the outside.
Woe to you, scribes and Pharisees, hypocrites! For you are like whitewashed tombs, which outwardly appear beautiful, but within are full of dead people's bones and all kinds of uncleanness.
So are you. From the outside you look like you're doing the right thing. But on the inside you're full of wrong. You pretend that you're not.
Woe to you, teachers of the law and you, Pharisees you hypocrites! You build tombs for the prophets and you decorate the tombs of the righteous.
And you said, "If we had been among the people of the past centuries, we would not have associated partners with God, nor would we have killed the prophets."
You testify against yourselves, acknowledging that you are the sons of those who kill the prophets.
Complete the sins that those before you began!
Oh, nest of poisonous wasps! How will you escape humiliation and the torment of Hell?
Therefore I am sending you prophets and wise men and teachers. Some of them you will kill and crucify, and some of them you will flog in your synagogues and persecute from town to town.
You will pay for every innocent drop of blood shed on earth, from the blood of righteous Abel to the blood of Zechariah son of Berekiah. Zechariah was the one I struck down between the temple and the altar.
What I am about to update you on is real, and it will affect those living now.
Jerusalem! Jerusalem! You who kill the prophets and stone those sent to you. How often I wanted to gather you like a hen gathers her chicks under her wings. But you would not let me!
Indeed, your dwelling is desolate, overturned upon its roofs.
I tell you, you will not see me again until you say, 'Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord' (Psalm 118:26)
Signs of the Hour
Jesus went out of the temple. And as he walked, his disciples came near to him. They wanted to call his attention to the structure of the temple.
« Is this not all new to you? » asked Jesus. « What I tell you is true. Not one stone will be left here upon the earth: every thing will be destroyed. »
Jesus was sitting on the Mount of Olives, and when the disciples went away with Him alone, they said, "Tell us, when will these things be, and what is the sign that these things are about to take place at the end of the age?" What is the sign that precedes your coming and the end of the age?"
Jesus answered: "Be watchful and cautious, lest you be deceived!"
Many will come in my name and say, 'I am the Messiah!' and they will lead many astray.
You will hear about wars. You will hear people talking about wars of the future too. Do not panic. These things must happen. But the end has not come yet.
One nation will fight against another nation, and one kingdom will fight against another kingdom, and the people will suffer from hunger, and there will be earthquakes in many places.
These are the beginning of labor pains.
At that time, people will deliver you over to be persecuted, and they will kill you, and you will be hated by all the nations because of my name.
And at that time many will fall away from the faith, and they will hate each other, and deliver up to slaughter one another.
Many false prophets will appear. They will mislead many people.
Because evil will multiply, so love will grow cold in most people.
